.Dd August 9, 2026
.Dt ANGEL 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm angel
.Nd friendlier CLI for managing macOS launchd services
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v | Fl \-verbose
.Op Fl y | Fl \-yes
.Ar command
.Op Ar options
.Op Ar args
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a macOS launchd service manager.
It wraps common
.Xr launchctl 1
workflows with clearer commands for installing, starting, stopping,
restarting, listing, inspecting, and logging services.
.Pp
Service names may be matched fuzzily unless
.Fl e Ns / Ns Fl \-exact
is given.
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v , Fl \-verbose
Verbose output.
.It Fl y , Fl \-yes
Assume yes for confirmation prompts.
.It Fl h , Fl \-help
Print help.
.It Fl V , Fl \-version
Print version.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss install
Install a service from a plist file (or resolve an existing daemon / bare
.Pa .plist
filename).
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm install
.Op Fl s | Fl \-strategy Ar strategy
.Op Fl \-domain Ar domain
.Ar path
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s , Fl \-strategy Ar strategy
How to place the plist:
.Ar copy ,
.Ar symlink
(default), or
.Ar move .
.It Fl \-domain Ar domain
Target domain:
.Ar gui ,
.Ar user ,
or
.Ar system .
Skips interactive domain selection.
.El
.Ss uninstall
Uninstall a service.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm uninstall
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss start
Start a service.
Alias:
.Cm kickstart .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm start
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Fl k | Fl \-kill
.Ar name
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl k , Fl \-kill
Kill any existing instance before starting.
.El
.Ss stop
Stop a service.
Alias:
.Cm kill .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm stop
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Fl s | Fl \-signal Ar signal
.Ar name
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl s , Fl \-signal Ar signal
Signal to send:
.Ar sigterm
(default),
.Ar sigkill ,
.Ar sighup ,
or
.Ar sigint .
.El
.Ss restart
Restart a service.
Alias:
.Cm kkill .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm restart
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss reboot
Boot out then bootstrap the service.
Reloads the plist from disk (picks up symlink target changes).
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm reboot
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss bootstrap
Bootstrap a service into launchd.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm bootstrap
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss bootout
Remove a service from launchd (bootout).
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm bootout
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss status
Show service status.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm status
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Fl d | Fl \-debug
.Ar name
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d , Fl \-debug
Show raw
.Xr launchctl 1
output and parsed data.
.El
.Ss logs
Show service logs.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm logs
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Fl t | Fl \-time Ar timeframe
.Ar name
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl t , Fl \-time Ar timeframe
Log time window, e.g.
.Ar 5m ,
.Ar 1h ,
.Ar 24h .
Default:
.Ar 5m .
.El
.Ss list
List services.
Alias:
.Cm ls .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm list
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Op Fl a | Fl \-apple
.Op Fl d | Fl \-dynamic
.Op Fl i | Fl \-idle
.Op Fl s | Fl \-sort Ar field
.Op Ar pattern
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a , Fl \-apple
Include Apple daemons.
.It Fl d , Fl \-dynamic
Include dynamically loaded daemons.
.It Fl i , Fl \-idle
Include idle daemons (no pid).
.It Fl s , Fl \-sort Ar field
Sort by
.Ar parent ,
.Ar domain ,
or
.Ar name
(default).
.El
.Ss plist
Print a service's plist.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm plist
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss enable
Enable a service.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm enable
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss disable
Disable a service.
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm disable
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Ss print
Print service information
.Pq Xr launchctl 1 Cm print wrapper .
.Pp
.Nm
.Cm print
.Op Fl e | Fl \-exact
.Ar name
.Sh COMMON OPTIONS
Most commands that take a service
.Ar name
accept:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl e , Fl \-exact
Require an exact name match instead of fuzzy matching.
.El
.Sh DOMAINS
.Nm
targets launchd domains the same way
.Xr launchctl 1
does:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ar gui
Aqua / GUI login session
.Pq Cm gui/$UID .
This is the
.Em default
for LaunchAgents in
.Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents
and
.Pa /Library/LaunchAgents
when the plist omits
.Cm LimitLoadToSessionType
(Apple's default is Aqua).
.It Ar user
Background / non-GUI user session
.Pq Cm user/$UID .
Use for agents meant for SSH-style contexts
.Pq typically Cm LimitLoadToSessionType=Background .
.It Ar system
System LaunchDaemons
.Pq Cm system .
Requires root.
.El
.Pp
.Nm
still honors an explicit
.Fl \-domain
on install and the plist's
.Cm LimitLoadToSessionType
when set
.Pq Aqua maps to gui; Background and LoginWindow map to user; System maps to system .
See also
.Xr launchctl 1
and Apple's
.Dq Daemons and Agents
technote
.Pq TN2083 .
.Sh CONFIGURATION
.Nm
optionally reads YAML config from the first existing path among:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
.Pa ~/.angelrc
.It
.Pa $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/angel/.angelrc
.It
.Pa ~/.config/angel/.angelrc
.El
.Pp
Config may define extra plist directories and their launchd domain:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
directories:
  - path: ~/Services
    domain: gui
  - path: /Library/LaunchDaemons
    domain: system
.Ed
.Pp
Valid
.Cm domain
values:
.Ar system ,
.Ar user ,
.Ar gui .
Paths may use
.Ql ~ .
Config is skipped when running as root
.Pq home is Pa /var/root .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
List user-visible services:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
angel list
.Ed
.Pp
Install a plist into the GUI domain via symlink:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
angel install ./com.example.my.plist --domain gui
.Ed
.Pp
Start, inspect, and stop a service:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
angel start my.service
angel status my.service
angel logs my.service -t 1h
angel stop my.service
.Ed
.Pp
Reload a service after editing a symlinked plist:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
angel reboot my.service
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr launchctl 1 ,
.Xr launchd 8
.Sh AUTHORS
.An The angel contributors
.Sh BUGS
